Dear Baroness Rock and Members of the Autism Act 2009 Committee,

=20

I am writing to submit formal evidence regarding systemic failures in the f=
amily justice system to uphold the participation duties required under FPR P=
art 3A and the Equality Act 2010. My case demonstrates how autism-related co=
mmunication and behavioural traits were misinterpreted as misconduct, and ho=
w disability participation measures were unlawfully revoked post-trial, resu=
lting in unfair and discriminatory findings.

=20

This evidence reveals a critical enforcement gap under the Autism Act 2009:=
 there is currently no statutory or independent mechanism enabling autistic =
or otherwise vulnerable court users to challenge non-compliance with partici=
pation duties. As Minister Stephen Kinnock MP recently confirmed to your Com=
mittee, =E2=80=9Cthere are no statutory powers of intervention=E2=80=A6 a failure could =
only be considered by the courts using judicial review.=E2=80=9D This leaves disab=
led parties without any practical means of redress when the courts themselve=
s fail to comply with their duties.

=20

The attached documentation is submitted as supplementary evidence for the C=
ommittee=E2=80=99s ongoing inquiry. It includes a detailed account of how judicial=
 reasoning in my case suppressed all reference to my autism and PTSD, despit=
e extensive medical and procedural evidence. This suppression created the fa=
ctual vacuum in which the Court miscast disability-linked traits as characte=
r flaws.

=20

I respectfully request that this submission be considered for inclusion in =
the Committee=E2=80=99s final report and recommendations, as it goes directly to t=
he heart of the Committee=E2=80=99s mandate: ensuring that the Autism Act 2009 pro=
vides real, enforceable protection for autistic people in practice, not only=
 in principle.

=20

This correspondence is also copied to the Ministry of Justice and HM Courts=
 & Tribunals Service for institutional accountability.

=20

I remain available to provide written or oral evidence to the Committee at =
short notice.

=20

Yours sincerely,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

=20

Attachments:

Letter to Baroness Rock =E2=80=93 Autism Act 2009 Committee (22 Oct 2025)

Pre-Action Protocol Letter (20 Oct 2025)

Follow-Up Letter on Unlawful Revocation of Participation Measures (21 Oct 2=
025)

Application Bundle CA-2024-001342 (Procedural Fairness and Equality Act Bre=
ach Evidence)

Letter from the Minister of State for Care to the Chair of the Committee (5=
 August 2025)

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20


